    rdfs:comment "The Int8 physical encoding: 8 bits / 1 bytes, endian-neutral. It interpretAs Integer — the integers ℤ, a subclass of Rational and superclass of Natural — the mutual-colimit back-pointer that closes the round-trip physical → interpretAs → formal reflexively onto its own formal type (spec §9d). It is signed (straddling zero). UEFI exact-width naming precedent: INT8. As a concrete bit-layout it fixes how a span of bits over the carrier is read as a value, and it byte-descends through the physical carrier ladder to the width-1 prim:Bit floor of the byte substrate." .

prim:Int16 a prim:PhysicalEncoding ;
